v850: fix word order of the 64-bit libgcc helpers

The DImode helpers in arch/v850/lib were copied from a big-endian
target and declare the high word first.  v850 is little-endian, so
__ashldi3, __ashrdi3, __lshrdi3 and __muldi3 mixed up the two halves:
shifts by 32 or more returned the wrong word and 64-bit products were
wrong.  Timekeeping (cyc2ns, xtime accumulation) and the jiffies
conversions use them, so the clock never advanced and every sleep hung.

diff -Nur linux-2.6.26.orig/arch/v850/lib/ashldi3.c linux-2.6.26/arch/v850/lib/ashldi3.c
--- linux-2.6.26.orig/arch/v850/lib/ashldi3.c	2026-11-21 11:43:51.734030658 +0100
+++ linux-2.6.26/arch/v850/lib/ashldi3.c	2026-11-21 11:43:51.736390477 +0100
@@ -25,7 +25,8 @@
 typedef		 int DItype	__attribute__ ((mode (DI)));
 typedef int word_type __attribute__ ((mode (__word__)));
 
-struct DIstruct {SItype high, low;};
+/* v850 is little-endian: the low word comes first.  */
+struct DIstruct {SItype low, high;};
 
 typedef union
 {
